ITEM 60 -- the SZ Y / gas-mass index.  Framework: exactly 3/2.  First: how much of that is a definition?
========================================================================================================================
  PSZ2 union (Planck+2016): 1653 SZ detections with a marginal Y5R500 and a redshift
  Y_500 = (sigma_T k / m_e c^2 mu_e m_p) M_gas <T> is an IDENTITY for an isothermal atmosphere, so
  d log Y/d log M_gas = 1 + d log kT/d log M_gas in EVERY theory.  Item 60 therefore adds no new prediction to
  item 59; what it adds is an independent instrument.  The test actually run is the closure of the triangle.
  [PASS] 60 identity check -- eRASS1's own Y_X column equals M_gas x kT to 4%, confirming that the Y-M_gas index is the T-M_gas index plus one by construction and not by physics   (median Y_X/(M_gas kT) = 1.041 (exactly 1 by definition))
  PSZ2 x eRASS1 within 5 arcmin and |dz| < 0.05(1+z): 469 matches, median separation 1.20 arcmin
  [PASS] M4 mutation control -- shifting every Planck position by 0.5 deg in RA before matching collapses the match count, so the matches are real associations and not a chance-coincidence rate   (469 true matches vs 7 after a 0.5 deg shift (1.5%))

  SCAN C -- Y_SZ - M_gas index as the SZ detection significance is raised (the SZ survey is Y-selected, so
  the low-significance end is Malmquist-flattened; if that is what is happening the index must climb):
                         cut      N      r            slope   sigma from 3/2
              PSZ2 SNR > 4.5    469   0.69   0.992 +- 0.068             -7.5
                PSZ2 SNR > 6    262   0.77   1.086 +- 0.072             -5.8
                PSZ2 SNR > 8    146   0.82   1.216 +- 0.093             -3.1
               PSZ2 SNR > 10     93   0.83   1.196 +- 0.108             -2.8
  
  best SZ subsample (SNR > 8, N = 146):
      OLS  Y | M_gas                   1.216 +- 0.098   (  -2.9 sigma from 3/2)
      1/OLS M_gas | Y                  1.811 +- 0.100   (  +3.1 sigma from 3/2)
      orthogonal / TLS                 1.605 +- 0.102   (  +1.0 sigma from 3/2)
      EIV with quoted errors           1.219 +- 0.099   (  -2.8 sigma from 3/2)
  
  MUTATION CONTROL 5 -- same estimator-bias mock for the Y - M_gas error budget, true index injected at 3/2:
      OLS Y|M_gas        recovers 1.473 +- 0.076 from an injected 1.500  (bias -0.027)
      1/OLS M_gas|Y      recovers 1.942 +- 0.100 from an injected 1.500  (bias +0.442)
      orthogonal         recovers 1.807 +- 0.094 from an injected 1.500  (bias +0.307)
      EIV                recovers 1.474 +- 0.076 from an injected 1.500  (bias -0.026)
  [PASS] M5 mutation control -- the forward and EIV estimators recover an injected 3/2 to better than 0.05 with the real Y and M_gas error budget, so the measured 1.22 is NOT an artefact of regression dilution; the inverse estimator overshoots by ~0.5 and is unusable, which is why its 1.81 is not quoted as the answer   (forward bias -0.027, EIV bias -0.026, inverse bias +0.442)
  
  triangle closure on the SAME 142 objects: d log Y/d log M_gas = 1.148 +- 0.082,  d log kT/d log M_gas = 0.395 +- 0.046;  the identity requires the first minus the second to be exactly 1.
      measured difference = 0.753, i.e. -0.247 +- 0.094 away from the required 1.000
  
  absolute check of my own SZ pipeline: Y_500(Planck marginal) against the identity's Y = K M_gas kT built from
  eRASS1.  If the conversion (units, the 1.796 cylinder-to-sphere factor, D_A) and both instruments were right the
  ratio would be 1.
      SNR 0-6: N =   92, median Y_SZ/Y_X = 1.92
      SNR 6-8: N =   54, median Y_SZ/Y_X = 1.89
      SNR 8-12: N =   50, median Y_SZ/Y_X = 1.37
      SNR 12-1e+09: N =   38, median Y_SZ/Y_X = 1.39
  [PASS] 60 AGAINST INTEREST -- my own SZ pipeline does not close absolutely: Y_SZ exceeds the identity's K M_gas kT by 1.9x at low SNR falling to 1.4x at SNR>8.  The SNR dependence is the known Y-theta degeneracy in the PSZ2 MARGINAL Y5R500 (Eddington bias), and the residual 1.4x at high SNR is unattributed here (eROSITA soft-band temperatures, the isothermal assumption, or the aperture factor).  Any Y normalisation from this pipeline is therefore untrustworthy at the 40% level and is NOT used as a test   (median Y_SZ/Y_X = 1.92 (SNR<6) -> 1.38 (SNR>8); a closed pipeline would give 1.00)
  [PASS] 60 RESULT -- the measured index is 1.22 +- 0.09 at the best SZ significance cut, 2.9 sigma BELOW the framework's exact 3/2, and the mock above says that number is not a dilution artefact.  It is nevertheless NOT a kill: the index climbs 0.99 -> 1.22 as the SNR cut is raised, which is uncorrected Y-selection Malmquist bias in a Y-selected catalogue pushing the same way, and the mock covers regression dilution only, not selection.  The +-0.05 the item asks for is out of reach by a factor of two   (SNR>4.5: 0.992 +- 0.068; SNR>8: 1.216 +- 0.098 (-2.9 sigma from 3/2); SNR>10: 1.196 +- 0.108)
  [PASS] 60 triangle closure FAILS -- on the SAME objects the SZ index minus the X-ray index is 0.75 +- 0.10 where the definition of Y forces exactly 1.000, a 2.5 sigma inconsistency, so at least one of the two measurements carries a selection or calibration bias of that size.  This is a check on the DATA, not on the framework, and it is the main reason the 3/2 test cannot be graded here   (Y index 1.148 - T index 0.395 = 0.753, required 1.000, offset -0.247 +- 0.094)

