SUMMARY
========================================================================================================================
  59  d log kT/d log M_gas, cluster regime, well-measured T:  eRASS1 0.493 +- 0.042,  eFEDS 0.507 +- 0.103
      framework 0.500 exactly; LambdaCDM chain 0.476-0.556 for f_gas slopes 0.20-0.40.  Consistent, NOT discriminating.
      groups included the index falls to 0.253 +- 0.007 -- open systematic, both sides.
      and the relation is not a pure power law at all in eRASS1: curvature +0.0647 +- 0.0053, which both
      the framework and self-similar LambdaCDM forbid; 1.2-1.4 sigma only in the two cleanest cuts, so unresolved.
      zero point buys one O(1) number: alpha_g = 1.18 (canonical) / 1.30 (alt), i.e. eta ~ 2.86-2.37.
  60  d log Y_SZ/d log M_gas = 0.992 +- 0.068 (SNR>4.5) rising to 1.216 +- 0.098 (SNR>8);
      framework 1.500 exactly, so -2.9 sigma; but the rise with the SNR cut is uncorrected SZ-selection bias
      pushing the same way, and the SZ/X-ray triangle does not close (-0.247 +- 0.094 from the required 1).
      and item 60 is item 59 + 1 by definition, so it was never an independent prediction to begin with.

